Took a quick shower, plan
on delivering this keynote,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.950
a couple of meetings,

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.850
and I'm heading to the airport at 4 p.m.,

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.780
so very quick trip,
unfortunately, this time,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.380
but I'm very excited about it.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.346
And there's a whole lot I wanna cover.

00:01:34.346 --> 00:01:38.040
So, let me create some context

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.450
for some of the people in the room

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.250
who don't know as much about me,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.250
and then I'll go into the reason why

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.410
I genuinely believe, as
we all sit here today

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:51.190
together, that because of this device

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.505
that many of you are holding,

00:01:53.505 --> 00:01:55.660
that we are living in the
most opportunistic time

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.330
every to put yourself
into a place of happiness,

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.710
and happiness comes in all forms.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.220
And I think a lot of business
and entrepreneurship,

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.220
but I definitely wanna articulate today

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:13.220
a framework that speaks
to how do you get happy

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.540
because of how much
opportunity there actually is.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.010
Let me take a step back.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.550
I was born in the Soviet Union in 1975

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.780
a little ways ago.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:28.060
I came to America when
I was three years old.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.810
It was a very challenging upbringing

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.010
in the first couple years.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:36.927
You know, six family members
in a studio apartment.

00:02:36.927 --> 00:02:40.050
We struggled, we had to
learn a new language.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.110
We started from the bottom, no question.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:46.630
As you can imagine, my parents
are very much my heroes.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.370
My mom stayed home and raised the kids.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.444
My dad worked every day,

00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:53.190
many, many, many hours a day.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.570
First, as a stock boy,

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.040
putting bottles on the shelf

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.250
in a liquor store in New Jersey

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.770
for only $2 an hour.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:05.236
So, very humble beginnings
where the Vaynerchuks come from,

00:03:05.236 --> 00:03:09.610
but entrepreneurship was
definitely foundational

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.900
in the happiness that
we were able to create

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.120
over that period of time.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.330
My dad worked quite a bit.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.410
Eventually, he became the
manager of that liquor store,

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.210
and that's when we moved to New Jersey,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.510
outside of New York City.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.440
And that's where I mainly grew up,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.703
and that's where my
entrepreneurial career began.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:33.700
I always wanted to work.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.490
You know, it came natural to me.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:36.480
It's what I wanted to do.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.290
When the summer days happened,

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.130
and all the kids wanted to play,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.350
I wanted to go wash people's cars.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.280
I wanted to sell lemonade.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.600
I wanted to do business.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.220
It was always in me.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.990
It's what made me happy.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.130
When I was five, six, seven years old,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.890
I convinced all my friends
to stand behind booths

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.500
from the lemonade that I made.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.030
And I would make signs,

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.060
and try to think about how to market.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.260
Long before the internet, I
cared about one core thing,

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.980
which was the attention of the person

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.770
that I was trying to reach,

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.480
and how I could get them
excited to buy my thing.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.363
Eventually, after lemonade,

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:19.060
I started my first,
kind of, real business.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.810
In America, in the 80's, baseball cards,

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.420
sports cards, that people could trade

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.390
became very, very big,

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.800
and I rode that wave.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.750
I got very involved.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.431
I loved sports, and I loved even more

00:04:31.431 --> 00:04:33.810
buying packs of cards, getting good cards,

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.960
and reselling them,

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.860
and that's really where I learned much.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.520
I mean, to think that sitting here today,

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.270
and having so many people clap for you,

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:48.230
on the complete other side of the world,

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:52.520
and so much of that was what I learned

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.090
in the malls and conventions in New Jersey

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.310
selling these cards, it's remarkable.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.180
I'm very humbled.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.670
I very much appreciate the warm welcome

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.210
when I came out here,

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.300
and I'm setting up this framework,

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.740
because I think, you know,

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.250
as I was getting ready
for this conference,

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.620
and I looked at so much of the chatter

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.970
about the conference,

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.930
and, obviously, the
phenomenal Instagram account

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.863
of our hosts, and kind of just looked,

00:05:18.863 --> 00:05:21.750
the thing that I become fascinated about,

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.480
and the thing that I
wanna talk about today

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.870
is really two things.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.100
Literally, right before I came out here,

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:30.890
with the organizers, they're
like, talk about the how,

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.467
and I asked them, I said, "The how, here,

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.536
"or the how here?"

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.860
(audience laughs)

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.790
What's interesting to
me now that I've been

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.190
a little older and had my career,

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.300
and I'll go back to it in a minute

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.950
to frame it up, but as I'm segwaying,

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.123
what's interesting to me is every

00:05:48.123 --> 00:05:51.590
wonderful person that
I'm looking at right now,

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:55.180
for them to get what they want, happiness.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.760
Forget about money for
a minute, happiness.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.000
For them to get what they want,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.930
it actually only is one of two things,

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.150
here or here.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.160
And here represents doing the work,

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.493
knowing what do.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.520
My whole career, as I got
more known on the internet,

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.660
I did not want to be a
motivational speaker,

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.080
and I spent many years
not talking about this.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.340
I mainly talked about this.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.083
But, after a while, what
started happening was

00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:28.300
I started reading enough comments,

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.210
'cause I read all my comments,

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.440
and I just started realizing so much

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:37.690
of why people can't get
there has to do with this,

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.430
that I started talking about it more

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.020
over the last four or five years,

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.620
but I think they both matter.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.720
You could be the most optimistic,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.630
happy person up here, but if you don't

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.730
put in the work, and if you don't know

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.800
what work to put in,
it's not gonna happen.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:57.424
Optimism is very close to delusion.

00:06:57.424 --> 00:06:59.900
(audience laughs)

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.240
However, I believe that
optimism is the fuel

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.390
to practicality, right?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.100
If you don't believe you're
doing it for a reason,

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.880
or it's exciting, you're not gonna want

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.380
to put in the hours of the work,

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.920
and so, that's who I've always been.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.180
I've always been ambitious and happy.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.350
I was very fortunate.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.770
I had a tremendous mother

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.410
who loved me very, very
much, so I felt good.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.530
However, she did not create entitlement.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.340
When I lost or I was
doing bad, she told me.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.410
She didn't make a fake environment,

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.558
which is a huge factor, and to be honest,

00:07:30.558 --> 00:07:33.868
my biggest concern about the
last 20 years of parenting,

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.970
too much fake environments,

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.920
too much entitlement,
which is why so many people

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.169
struggle when they go into the real world

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.390
because the real world doesn't care.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.323
The real world is not your mama anymore,

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.403
and so, I think about those things.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.100
Fast forward, I was very good
at selling baseball cards.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.300
When you're making three
or $4,000 a weekend

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.770
when you're 14 years old, you've got it.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.130
I was good, fine, but then my dad,

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.510
eventually, bought a liquor store,

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:03.160
and he dragged me into the liquor store

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.740
when I was 14.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.540
I started making two
bucks an hour bagging ice.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:09.970
This was huge for me.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.610
If I didn't have that transition,

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.280
all the money I was making as a young kid,

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.961
it came so easy 'cause I
was naturally talented.

00:08:16.961 --> 00:08:20.540
I think not having that
struggle of losing all that

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.750
because my dad forced
me to work in the store,

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.670
and making $20 a day,
that really helped me,

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.750
and I learned a lot in that liquor store.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.440
Most of all, what I learned
was to watch people.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.610
Today, after this talk,
I will go to the airport,

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.820
and on my flight, I will, literally,

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:41.090
read most of the comments on Twitter,

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.900
on Instagram, your DMs, I will read them,

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:46.320
and I'll read them to understand

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.480
was there anything I
said in said in this hour

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.422
that stood out, that
didn't hit, that did hit.

00:08:51.422 --> 00:08:54.150
I learned that watching people,

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.210
and more importantly,
understanding people,

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:59.650
and most importantly,
being empathetic to people,

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.830
was the best way to build a real business,

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:02.930
to build something meaningful.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.850
The biggest problem,
I'll tell you right now,

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.060
one of the biggest reasons
most people in this room,

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.020
if they decide to start an
entrepreneurial venture,

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:13.610
a side hustle, whether you try to sell

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.300
something in your home
on Facebook Marketplace,

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.330
which, oh, by the way,
I'm gonna bring up later.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.420
My biggest believe that the quickest way

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.670
for many people here to start is to sell

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.560
stuff on Facebook Marketplace.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.860
But I'll talk about that later.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.660
Whether it's that, whether
you're finally ready

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.790
to start your podcast on Spotify,

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:34.268
whether you're gonna build
your Instagram profile,

00:09:34.268 --> 00:09:38.180
or meme page because
you want brand dollars,

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.170
whatever you're up to in this room,

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:44.690
the reality is that if you have to put in

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:48.790
so much work, but so
much of what comes out

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.156
of people's mouth, or what they post

00:09:51.156 --> 00:09:56.156
is selfish not selfless.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.470
It's what you want.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:58.960
You want them to buy it.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.740
You want them to like your post.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.570
You want them to follow you.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:04.500
The biggest reason I have the luxury

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.090
of standing here today,

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.690
is from the wine business,

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:11.045
to the content I made on
YouTube when it first came out,

00:10:11.045 --> 00:10:14.520
to everything I've done over
the last eight to nine years,

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.223
in my books, in all my free content,

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.830
I've always thought how do
I bring more value to you

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.760
than I get in return?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.150
It's very simple.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:29.260
Karma, or doing the
right thing always works.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:33.050
The problem is most people are impatient.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.980
The reason most people are impatient,

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:39.890
especially, in cultures
like mine, Eastern European,

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.700
in cultures like here,

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.860
there's too many people in here

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:47.020
that are trying to get successful too fast

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:49.403
because they wanna prove
it to their parents.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:56.230
And in that impatience,
is a very important point.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:11:01.230
My friends, the number
one thing I fear, period,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.270
is that people live their lives

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.313
based on other people's opinions.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.190
The number one thing that I have seen,

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:10.740
as I have gotten older, that has been

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.140
very obvious to me,

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.080
is that most of the people here today,

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.230
do many of the things they do

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:20.490
because of one to five people's
opinions in their lives,

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.350
whether their parents, their spouse,

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.630
their older sibling, their neighbor.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:27.240
Living your life predicated

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:31.130
on the judgment of somebody else,

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.990
is the great weakness of the human being.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.770
The biggest reason, do you know how many

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:40.240
people are here today
just to get affirmation

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.650
from me to go and do something?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.040
(audience laughs)

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.390
I mean it.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.220
I mean it, and it's fascinating to me,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:51.770
and I'm empathetic, I understand,

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.110
and I want to talk about it a lot,

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:56.940
because no matter how
I tell you how to leave

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.778
500 comments on Instagram posts,

00:11:59.778 --> 00:12:02.930
or what time to post your posts,

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:06.550
or why you should start a
Spotify podcast tomorrow,

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:10.580
or how you actually list an
item on Facebook Marketplace,

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.390
no matter what I tell you,

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.670
if you post the first day,

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.570
and the person that you're worried about

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.530
has a bad opinion of it,

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.903
it's already game over.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.200
And so, I flew all the way here,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.470
24 hours, to put pressure
on what is the most

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.752
obvious conversation, which is,

00:12:31.752 --> 00:12:36.752
are you prepared to finally
get quiet in your head

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.640
and not allow the opinions of others

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.630
to dictate your behaviors?

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:44.030
Every person here knows
what they want to do.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.363
If you're here today,

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.860
there's something
running through your mind

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:48.950
that you want to do.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.220
There's no reason for you to be here today

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.220
unless there's something
running through your mind

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:55.443
that you want to do.

00:12:57.114 --> 00:12:59.420
How many people here
are over 40 years old?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.660
Raise your hands, raise them high.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.366
Raise high, don't be scared, raise high.

00:13:04.366 --> 00:13:06.770
(audience laughs)

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.855
Jesus Christ, this is a young crowd.

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.904
(audience laughs)

00:13:11.904 --> 00:13:15.821
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.360
For the very small percentage of us here

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.437
that are over 40--
- Yeah.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:24.469
- Thanks, brother.

00:13:24.469 --> 00:13:26.080
(audience laughs)

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.529
There's like eight of us, bro.

00:13:27.529 --> 00:13:29.360
(audience laughs)

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.793
For, like, the 11 of us,

00:13:31.793 --> 00:13:35.303
look, here's, this is a lot of fun,

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:41.200
for the 11 of us, we
lived life before this.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.370
We were grown.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:45.410
We were grownups already
before the internet came.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:46.480
I was 18 years old.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.390
I'd lived my life, at least,

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.800
the childhood part of my
life, without the internet.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:54.060
The biggest thing that excites me,

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.387
especially in a mature
internet market like here,

00:13:56.387 --> 00:13:59.260
WhatsApp, and Facebook, and Instagram,

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.590
and YouTube, and Spotify, like,

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:05.070
there's so much opportunity,

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:07.970
and you don't even have
to leave your home.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:11.260
There's no building your life, you know,

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.650
after hours, when I was growing up.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.960
When you had a job, and you
had to take care of something,

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:19.210
you didn't then start another
job because it was late,

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.930
but, now, this allows it.

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.650
The biggest thing that I wanna get across

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.470
in this little moment of this speech,

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:29.720
is everybody in here is
taking this for granted.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.620
Your grandparents, your
great-grandparents,

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.680
your great-great grandparents,
they didn't have this.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.650
If you aren't succeeding, or attacking

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:40.963
your success with this in your hand,

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.233
then what are you doing?

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.513
Every single person
here has the opportunity

00:14:47.513 --> 00:14:50.730
to create a profile

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:52.570
and a presence online

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.770
whether it's yourself, or your business,

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:59.423
or your idea, and the
cost is (clicks) zero.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:02.450
I love when people get made when Facebook

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:06.570
or Instagram's organic reach goes down.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.773
I keep reminding them it's free.

00:15:10.121 --> 00:15:13.330
(audience laughs)

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.700
How many people here are on Instagram?

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.533
Raise your hand.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.720
Jesus.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:22.940
(audience laughs)

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:24.860
Over the next year or two,

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.530
Instagram's reach is gonna go down

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.493
because more ads are going to go in.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.340
So, as you can imagine, I'm so passionate

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.960
to get you to post three
or four times a day,

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.940
not once a day, yet, everybody
overthinks their posts,

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:43.580
so much, 'cause there's so scared not get

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.133
as many likes as they did last time.

00:15:46.133 --> 00:15:49.481
(audience laughs)

00:15:49.481 --> 00:15:51.810
It's true, it's 100% true.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:54.220
The amount of people here
who want to post something,

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.840
but retake it 53 times.

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:59.780
(audience laughs)

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.910
Or change the filter, or
things of that nature,

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.680
or, my favorite move, you post it,

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.730
but in the first 83 seconds,

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.384
you don't get enough
likes, and you remove it.

00:16:09.384 --> 00:16:12.830
(audience laughs)

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.950
It's a fascinating thing for me to watch

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.220
because what it speaks
to is, in my opinion,

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:21.040
people being confused about the game.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.930
I view the game macro.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.460
I watch most people play micro.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.423
You're not in the business of
getting likes on Instagram.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.930
Yet, you're pandering
to the machine of that.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.290
You're in the business
of creating awareness

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:37.690
for whatever you want.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.860
You want people to know
what you want them to know,

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.270
whatever that may be,

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.570
business, raise money for a charity,

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.360
sell something, become a personal brand.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.200
You know, whatever it might be.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:49.060
(audience laughs)

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:51.450
Whatever it might be,
that's what you want,

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:54.530
yet, people get so caught
up in the semantics.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:57.150
Listen, what I can tell
you from my career,

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.900
is this repeats over,
and over, and over again.

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:04.900
In 2006, I started one of the
first YouTube shows, period.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:08.260
It was the longest show on
YouTube when I launched it.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.990
YouTube wasn't even a year old.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:11.560
I sat in front of a camera,

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:13.780
and I drank wine for 30 minutes,

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.525
and a lot of people watched it.

00:17:15.525 --> 00:17:17.690
(audience laughs)

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:19.450
A year later, Twitter came out,

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:21.480
and I was one of the first
people to move on that.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.779
I invested because I got
smarter at that point,

00:17:23.779 --> 00:17:26.430
but I also was one of the first people

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:29.320
to amass a million
followers on that platform.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.890
Before I did YouTube and Twitter,

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:33.507
a year or two earlier, in America

00:17:33.507 --> 00:17:35.170
and many other parts of the world,

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:38.290
MySpace had won and dominated,

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.870
and there were people
that won on that platform.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.290
If you pay attention to
what happened on MySpace,

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.500
if you pay attention to
what happened on YouTube,

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.160
if you pay attention to
what happened on Twitter,

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.560
and then Facebook, and then Vine,

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.270
and on, and on, and on,

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:53.950
it's all the same game.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.980
In the beginning, if you move quickly,

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.180
you can get more attention.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.370
Most people get frustrated
that they aren't first,

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.210
and they don't go all in

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:05.790
'cause they think they missed it.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:09.230
However, winning on these platforms

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.873
is a game of being better, not first.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.640
Being better comes in two ways.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:18.280
This is where it gets very
important, my friends.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.530
Being better on putting out content

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:23.400
only comes out in two ways.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.930
Either, entertainment, right?

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:29.280
Or information.

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:31.540
If you are putting out
content on these websites,

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.228
and trying to grow,

00:18:33.228 --> 00:18:36.290
and you want to succeed
and build an audience,

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:38.193
you either do information,

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.900
you know what you're talking about,

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.533
whether it's painting nails, business,

00:18:43.533 --> 00:18:46.440
wine, sneakers, hair care.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.060
I don't care what it is.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.800
You either know or you entertain.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.120
Entertainment comes in a lot of ways.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:54.810
This is playing out on Instagram.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.530
Entertainment comes in being funny.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:00.370
Entertainment comes in being musical.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.840
Entertainment and escapism
comes in being attractive,

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:04.800
being a model.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:09.130
It all plays, if you're
lucky enough to have both,

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.900
it gets really crazy.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:13.820
But if you do not do one
or the other, you lose.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:17.360
If you go look at your
Instagram account right now,

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:19.910
and look at the last 10 posts,

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:22.370
my question to you is very simple,

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:25.190
did you post those posts for your audience

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.890
so they could be entertained or informed,

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.920
or did you post it for yourself,

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:35.102
for your own self-esteem, or insecurities?

00:19:35.102 --> 00:19:36.570
(audience laughs)

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.220
Let me save you time.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.152
You posted it for yourself.

00:19:40.152 --> 00:19:43.620
(audience laughs)

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:46.420
The biggest take away that
you could have from here,

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:47.930
in my opinion, is a couple of things.

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:50.590
Number one, you are very fortunate

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:54.630
to live in a country with
disproportionate advances

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.890
on these platforms.

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:59.043
When I look at the data
of how much attention

00:19:59.043 --> 00:20:01.970
is on this device, and those six platforms

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.220
in this country, and the
size of this country,

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.120
it is staggering.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.440
This is one of the best places

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:11.100
in the world to produce
content for YouTube,

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.460
Spotify, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.902
It's one of the best places in the world.

00:20:15.902 --> 00:20:18.950
(audience applauds)

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.020
See, you did it again.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.666
You clapped for yourself.

00:20:21.666 --> 00:20:24.010
(audience laughs)

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:25.800
Oh, actually fun fact.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.760
Actually, back to this amazing place,

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.473
and the internet, and apps.

00:20:30.327 --> 00:20:31.610
I don't know if a lot of you know this,

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:35.380
but I was one of the first
five investors in Path,

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:38.180
which was a huge app here
for a long period of time

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.410
before it shut down a year ago.

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:42.050
So because I was an
early investor in Path,

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.670
and because this became
the biggest market for Path

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.990
four or five years ago,

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:49.240
I spent a lot of time paying
attention to this market

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:52.690
from far away, and what
I can tell you is this,

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.920
the beauty of the people that live here,

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:58.720
and it's funny, there's
so much amazingness.

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:00.330
You know, in the world that I see,

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.900
how many people here consume my content?

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:03.750
Raise your hands.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.673
Thank you, so, thank you.

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:10.313
So, if you do, you have
a good sense of me.

00:21:10.313 --> 00:21:13.280
You can imagine why I
love Indonesia so much.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:17.310
All the love, and optimism,
and warmth plays out here,

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.830
but the biggest thing I'm passionate about

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.340
is getting people to be less insecure,

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.140
and care less about what people think,

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:27.440
especially their parents,
plays out here, too.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:30.560
And so, for me, it's a really
interesting market to look at

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.090
with trends and how people do things,

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.320
and what they respond to,

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.070
and who they follow, and why,

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:38.533
and so what I can tell you is

00:21:38.533 --> 00:21:41.750
if you are capable, if you are capable

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.110
to be strong enough, internally,

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.891
to start posting on these platforms,

00:21:46.891 --> 00:21:50.500
more truth, more your truth,

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.730
you, you're truth, you will
see a remarkable return

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:56.633
on that investment in this market.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:01.580
Now, let's talk about content

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.860
because no matter what
you're doing in this room,

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.300
you're gonna have to produce it

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.120
to achieve what you want.

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:10.780
The problem is there's a lot
of ways to produce content.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:14.680
One of the biggest issues that
I'm excited to address here

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:17.160
is a world where Instagram
does extremely well,

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:19.760
or YouTube, people think
pictures and videos

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:21.400
are the only way to go.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.050
I'm here to tell you
that two of the places

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:28.456
that I'm most excited about
are the written word and audio.

00:22:28.456 --> 00:22:30.190
(audience member cheers)

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:34.330
If you are not comfortable
taking tons of pictures

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:36.420
and videos, you immediately have to make

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:37.740
a decision here today.

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:39.720
Are you a good writer?

00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:42.160
And if you are, I have a
lot of good news for you.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.170
I'll go to that in a minute.

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:45.460
Or, two, if you like to talk,

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:47.501
however you're uncomfortable with video,

00:22:47.501 --> 00:22:49.990
I couldn't be, back to your clapping,

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:54.210
more passionate about the last six months,

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:58.090
in Indonesia, the
consumption of podcasting

00:22:58.090 --> 00:23:00.009
in this country is exploding.

00:23:00.009 --> 00:23:03.009
(audience applauds)

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:09.210
The unbelievable ease to produce a podcast

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:13.150
and distribute it in 2019 is remarkable.

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:14.990
There's an app I've been
talking about a long time.

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:18.170
It just got bought by
Spotify, called Anchor.

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:19.760
It's called Anchor.

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:21.240
You can download it on your phone.

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:23.070
You literally record on your phone.

00:23:23.070 --> 00:23:24.560
You press two more buttons,

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:27.570
and it puts it all over
to the different podcasts.

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:28.780
No friction.

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:31.120
You could be doing it right now.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.780
So, the excuse of I
don't know how to do it,

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:34.810
or how do I produce it,

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:36.800
or do I have to go to the radio station?

00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:37.880
And how do I?

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.990
Nothing, cost of entry, zero.

00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:42.870
Friction, zero.

00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:45.080
Literally, all you have to do is Google,

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:46.670
how do I use Anchor?

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:47.963
Or download it.

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:52.940
I highly recommend if
you have something to say

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.165
about some category, I highly recommend

00:23:56.165 --> 00:23:58.430
getting very serious about podcasts.

00:23:58.430 --> 00:24:00.690
'Cause I believe that audio,

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:02.320
over the next decade, is going to be

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:04.660
one of the biggest ways we consume

00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:08.040
because we don't like wasting time.

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.290
Humans love efficiency.

00:24:10.290 --> 00:24:12.820
And audio saves time.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:14.950
Audio's exploding, and
will continue to explode,

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:17.800
and I highly recommend
you look at it seriously.

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:20.140
Another thing that's interesting to me

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:23.870
is actually a little tidbit
I don't share very often,

00:24:23.870 --> 00:24:27.100
but I always say, "Watch
what I do, not what I say."

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:28.880
When I looked at the
hashtags or the comments

00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:31.660
for this conference, I looked
at a bunch of accounts.

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.150
The number one mistake I believe people

00:24:34.150 --> 00:24:36.050
are doing on Instagram right now,

00:24:36.050 --> 00:24:38.283
is not leaving enough written copy.

00:24:39.770 --> 00:24:42.550
If you look at my posts,

00:24:42.550 --> 00:24:44.850
when I post a picture
or video on Instagram,

00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:46.223
I write a lot of copy.

00:24:47.130 --> 00:24:49.330
I don't do that for my health.

00:24:49.330 --> 00:24:51.950
I don't like wasting three minutes.

00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:54.180
I do it 'cause it matters.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:58.230
So, I know a lot of you are
trying to build your Instagram.

